       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6d51465aa828084aeddbf6d03c81fdc4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAW-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Andrew Woods",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=60785ded115da6006f540529",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>I believe the previous behavior was that if you deleted an Non-RDF-Description, the Binary was also deleted. Likewise, if you deleted a Binary, the Non-RDF-Description was also deleted. <br/>\nI would suggest we disallow the deletion of Non-RDF-Descriptions, since they are auto-created, and are in a sense \"server-managed\".<br/>\n\"405 Method Not Allowed\" seems apprpriate.</p>",
     "created": "03/May/19 7:02 PM",
     "id": "20675",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/12937/comment/20675",
